# Context-aware cinematics

Use the cinematic engine for:

- rare drops
- skill levels
- Slayer levels
- achievements
- personal bests
- expensive purchases
- first completions
- goal completion
- joke deaths
- friend-group milestones
- cosmetic unlocks
- title unlocks

During Dungeons, Kuudra, boss phases, or dangerous combat:

- do not play intrusive cinematics
- optionally show compact notification
- queue the full event
- play after leaving the activity
- merge similar events
- expire stale events
- show recap instead of spam

Example recap:

Dungeon complete

3 queued events:
- rare drop
- Catacombs level-up
- achievement unlocked

# Resume where I left off

On login or reconnect, show a useful resume card only if meaningful state exists.

Possible content:

- previous activity
- active goal
- last meaningful action
- current progress
- last-used gear/pet
- active waypoint
- unfinished timer
- queued events
- suggested next action
- whether the previous session ended unexpectedly

Do not show pointless summaries such as “you were standing in Hub.”

